        }
      ],
      "updated": 1785695221059,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "NOTE: If you're wondering, \"What if the TCP header contains\noptions?\" don't worrry. The TCP payload can be LESS THAAN or\nEQUAAL to the MSS, but never greater. So, if we have something in\noptions, the  TCP payload will always be LESS THAN MSS",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "NOTE: If you're wondering, \"What if the TCP header contains options?\" don't worrry. The TCP payload can be LESS THAAN or EQUAAL to the MSS, but never greater. So, if we have something in options, the  TCP payload will always be LESS THAN MSS",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
